cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: >-
  cairn: committee-tower threshold ML-DSA-65 signing for proof-of-stake
  checkpoints
abstract: >-
  Research implementation in which a quorum of validators jointly produces one
  standard ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) signature over a finalized checkpoint, verified
  by unmodified FIPS 204 code. Sixteen signers in nested 3-of-4 committees
  compress their key shares into a three-party additive sharing; a three-party
  MPC (MP-SPDZ) evaluates the exact FIPS 204 ExpandMask, the rounding functions
  and the abort checks. Includes a multi-process implementation over mutual
  TLS, an integration with the PQC Sidecar checkpoint daemon, and measurements
  on one host and across two hosts. Research artifact; not production
  cryptography.
authors:
